-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Santos</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Viral causes of the acute retinal necrosis syndrome</article-title><source>Am J Ophthalmol</source><volume>129</volume><fpage>166</fpage><lpage>72</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10682968</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b7-co-2-451"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Han</surname><given-names>DP</given-names></name><name><surname>Lewis</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1987</year><article-title>Laser photocoagulation in the acute retinal necrosis syndrome</article-title><source>Arch Ophthalmol</source><volume>105</volume><fpage>1051</fpage><lpage>4</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3632413</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b8-co-2-451"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Khurana</surname><given-names>RN</given-names></name><name><surname>Charonis</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Samuel</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Intravenous foscarnet in the management of acyclovir-resistant herpes simplex virus type 2 in acute retinal necrosis in children</article-title><source>Med Sci Monit</source><volume>11</volume><fpage>75</fpage><lpage>8</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b9-co-2-451"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Knox</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Chandler</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Short</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Polymerase chain reaction-based assays of vitreous samples for the diagnosis of viral retinitis</article-title><source>Ophthalmology</source><volume>105</volume><fpage>37</fpage><lpage>45</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9442777</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b10-co-2-451"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kolacny</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Stalmans</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Wouters</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Bilateral acute retinal necrosis in a 12-year-old girl</article-title><source>J AAPOS</source><volume>9</volume><fpage>599</fpage><lpage>601</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16414533</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b11-co-2-451"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nakanishi</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Takahashi</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Ibaraki</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Acute retinal necrosis with varicella zoster dermatitis in the fellow eyelid</article-title><source>Nippon Ganka Gakkai Zasshi</source><volume>103</volume><fpage>477</fpage><lpage>81</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10410561</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b12-co-2-451"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schlingemann</surname><given-names>RO</given-names></name><name><surname>Bruinenberg</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Wertheim-van Dillen</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Twenty years&#x02019; delay of fellow eye involvement in herpes simplex virus type 2-associated bilateral acute retinal necrosis syndrome</article-title><source>Am J Ophthalmol</source><volume>122</volume><fpage>891</fpage><lpage>2</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8956648</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b13-co-2-451"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tan</surname><given-names>JCHD</given-names></name><name><surname>Byles</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Stanford</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Acute retinal necrosis in children caused by herpes simplex virus</article-title><source>Retina</source><volume>21</volume><fpage>344</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11508880</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b14-co-2-451"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tran</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name><name><surname>Stanescu</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Caspers-Velu</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Clinical characteristics of acute HSV-2 retinal necrosis</article-title><source>Am J Ophthalmol</source><volume>137</volume><fpage>872</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15126152</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b15-co-2-451"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Urayama</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamada</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Sasaki</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><year>1971</year><article-title>Unilateral acute uveitis with retinal periarteritis and detachment</article-title><source>Jpn J Clin Ophthalmol</source><volume>25</volume><fpage>607</fpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b16-co-2-451"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zajdenweber</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Muccioli</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Interventions for acute retinal necrosis</article-title><source>Cochrane Database Syst Rev</source><volume>3</volume><fpage>CD004505</fpage></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="f1-co-2-451" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Retinography at the first examination showing the vitreous body inflammation and retinal periphlebitis. The initial vision was &#x0003c;20/400 in both eyes.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="co-2-451f1"/></fig><fig id="f2-co-2-451" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>In detail, the retinography displays normal appearance of the macula and optic disc.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="co-2-451f2"/></fig><fig id="f3-co-2-451" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Control retinography in the third week. The final visual acuity was 20/200 OD and 20/400 OS.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="co-2-451f3"/></fig><table-wrap id="t1-co-2-451" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Patient characteristics</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Age/sex</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Affected eye</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Initial AVOD, AVOI</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Initial symptoms</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Inicial fundus signs</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Diagnostic lab probes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5 years Male</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Both</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;20/400</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Red eyes<break/>Light sensitivity<break/>Impaired vision</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Bilateral ischaemic retina<break/>Perivasculitis, Retinal edema<break/>Vascular thrombosis<break/>Vitritis<break/>No papillary affection</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">IgM anti-EBV (<bold>+</bold>)<break/>IgG anti-EBV (&#x02212;)<break/>CMV (&#x02212;)<break/>HSV (&#x02212;)<break/>HIV (&#x02212;)<break/>Toxoplasma (&#x02212;)<break/>Chlamydia pneumoniae/psitacci (&#x02212;)<break/>Borrellia (&#x02212;)<break/>Brucella (&#x02212;)<break/>Mycoplasma (&#x02212;)<break/>Treponema(&#x02212;)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Personal history</bold></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Fever</bold></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Final AVOD, AVOI</bold></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Final symptoms</bold></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Final fundus signs</bold></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Final treatment</bold></td></tr><tr><td colspan="6" align="left" rowspan="1"><hr/></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Oral aphtas</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Yes</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">20/40</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">None</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Scarce pigmented scars</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Intravenous acyclovir (Zovirax<sup>&#x000ae;</sup>)<break/>Acetil salicylic acid (Aspirin<sup>&#x000ae;</sup>)<break/>Ciclopentolate eye drops</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn1-co-2-451"><p><bold>Abbreviations:</bold> EBV, Epstein-Barr virus; IgG, immunoglobulin G; IgM, immunoglobulin M.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>